# ADM-Cube Paper accounts: the pre-open order sheet of every SSE session, per book.
# Install or refresh with: /home/lzp/miniconda3/envs/quant/bin/python ops/cron/install_cron.py --block paper
#
# Books live in data/trading/paper/<book>/ (run_paper.py init). Each run goes
# through every book in turn: it settles the sessions whose data has been
# committed, decides today's session at its inference time (08:00 unless the
# book's experiment set another) and writes
# logs/paper/<book>/<date>_orders.md plus that book's latest_orders.md. A book
# that cannot decide writes the reason to the same files and the run continues
# with the next book, exiting non-zero if any book failed. Weekday holidays
# exit at once. The books that ask for no GPU run first, then the GPU books;
# within each group the books the owner trades by hand -- the ones he switched
# to real fills -- run first, so their sheets are ready before the others; this
# file names no book, so books can come and go without editing it.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
CRON_TZ=Asia/Shanghai
REPO_ROOT=/Data2/lzp/auto-trade
QUANT_PYTHON=/home/lzp/miniconda3/envs/quant/bin/python

# The operator places the sheet's orders by hand: an order that fills at the
# open goes into the 09:15-09:25 opening call auction, one that fills at the
# close into the 14:57-15:00 closing call auction. Every sheet is due at 09:10,
# five minutes before the opening auction, whatever its book's decision time;
# the decision time stays the moment the strategy's data is as of, wherever in
# the morning the run falls.
#
# The runs work back from 09:10 (PAPER_SHEET_DUE in src/autotrade/paper/book.py)
# with a 75-minute budget for one attempt: the strategy container's start
# clock (15 min) plus the Paper decision clock (60 min,
# PAPER_DECISION_TIMEOUT_SECONDS, one decision call in every book, whatever its
# experiment's). A book's whole run -- its PIT build, the replay of its earlier
# decisions and one decision -- takes 8-13 min on a quiet host and 42 min
# measured with four research experiments on the box. Books run one after another.
# The clocks bound each call, not the run: a run that ends after 09:10 still
# writes its sheet -- the same decision, too late for the opening auction.
#
# 05:40 is the first, after the nightly chain has committed the previous
# session: the evening update (23:35, visible from 03:05), the intraday-flow
# build (02:45), the PIT event build (03:35), the revision sentinel (04:00) and
# the text audit (05:00). It has the slack for a refit day, when the fit adds
# 10-40 min, capped at the fit timeout init froze into that book's book.json
# from its experiment's strategy_fit_timeout_seconds; the last retry's budget
# does not cover a fit.
#
# 06:40 and 07:55 are retries for a morning whose data landed late or whose
# first run was slow: flock skips a retry while an earlier run is still
# working, and a book whose session is already decided is a no-op re-render,
# never a second decision. 07:55 is the last that still has the budget before
# 09:10, and it follows the latest the PIT event build has run; 06:40 is a
# budget before it, so a 06:40 retry that runs one book in full has ended when
# the last one starts. The PIT event build is the part of the chain that can
# push past 05:40 under load (03:35-05:32 on a quiet night, 03:35-07:14 on
# 2026-09-16 with four experiments running); a night where it runs past 07:55
# needs the experiments throttled, not another retry.
#
# A GPU book takes its card only as its strategy container starts; with no
# eligible card it looks again every 60 s until 135 min after its run began
# (run_paper.py --gpu-poll-seconds / --gpu-wait-minutes), so the 05:40 run keeps
# looking until 07:55, when the last retry starts: a card found at its last
# look still leaves the budget before the sheet is due. A run waiting for
# a card is still working: the retries skip while it waits, so a book that
# failed in it for late data is retried only after it ends, or by hand with
# run_paper.py run --book <book>.
40 5 * * 1-5 cd $REPO_ROOT && mkdir -p logs/paper .runtime/paper && flock -n .runtime/paper/cron.lock $QUANT_PYTHON scripts/paper/run_paper.py run >> logs/paper/cron.log 2>&1
40 6 * * 1-5 cd $REPO_ROOT && mkdir -p logs/paper .runtime/paper && flock -n .runtime/paper/cron.lock $QUANT_PYTHON scripts/paper/run_paper.py run >> logs/paper/cron.log 2>&1
55 7 * * 1-5 cd $REPO_ROOT && mkdir -p logs/paper .runtime/paper && flock -n .runtime/paper/cron.lock $QUANT_PYTHON scripts/paper/run_paper.py run >> logs/paper/cron.log 2>&1
